  "title": "Hrana i piće",
  "titleEn": "Food and Drink",
  "grammarTip": "The accusative case marks the direct object — what you eat or drink. Feminine nouns ending in -a change that ending to -u: voda → Pijem vodu (I drink water), kafa → Pijem kafu. Masculine and neuter nouns for inanimate things keep the same form as the nominative: hljeb → Jedem hljeb, meso → Jedem meso. The verbs 'jesti' (to eat) and 'piti' (to drink) always take their object in the accusative: Šta jedeš? Jedem sir. Šta piješ? Pijem sok.",
